{"availability":"available","full":"JonasJavier/wikiverse","name":"wikiverse","description":"Wikiverse — a modern, open encyclopedia. Django REST Framework + React 19, with full revision history, word-level diffs, talk pages and Postgres full-text search.","category":"Design","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2024-04-22T23:49:48Z","updated":"2026-10-05T10:24:13Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://wikiverse.jonasjavier.dev","topics":["cs50w","django","django-rest-framework","encyclopedia","full-stack","full-text-search","portfolio","postgresql","python","railway","react","redis","search","tailwindcss","typescript","vite","wiki","wikipedia"],"demo":"https://wikiverse.jonasjavier.dev/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:00.287Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:00.287Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:00.287Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T15:38:00.287Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Revision history, word-level diffs, talk pages, watchlists, citations, red links and PostgreSQL full-text search — the machinery of a real wiki, without MediaWiki.","Live site · API reference · Architecture · Design decisions","Wikiverse began as the wiki assignment of Harvard's CS50's Web Programming with Python and JavaScript and was rebuilt into a production application. It models what makes a wiki a wiki: every save is an immutable revision, any two revisions can be compared word by word, every article has a talk page, and a link to an article nobody has written yet shows up red and opens the editor with the title already filled in."],"features":["Reference-work layout: lead section, infobox, lead image with licence credit, See also","Numbered footnotes that link both ways, and a formatted reference list","Hover previews on every wikilink; red links for unwritten articles","Sticky table of contents with scroll-spy, a Tools rail and a print stylesheet","Main page with a featured article, Did you know… and On this day"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JonasJavier/wikiverse/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e0a6974032c1152bd8a17eaac4e21609a12c3c41227ba6ff0240f322dc7f5e76","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:00.469Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:00.469Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Revision history, word-level diffs, talk pages, watchlists, citations, red links and PostgreSQL full-text search — the machinery of a real wiki, without MediaWiki.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JonasJavier/wikiverse/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"A strict Content Security Policy is emitted by both nginx and Django, fonts are self-hosted, remote images are allowlisted, JWT refresh tokens rotate and are revocable, and login throttles cannot be reset by spoofing X-Forwarded-For.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JonasJavier/wikiverse/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"e0a6974032c1152bd8a17eaac4e21609a12c3c41227ba6ff0240f322dc7f5e76","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JonasJavier/wikiverse/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:00.469Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-05T10:24:13Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JonasJavier/wikiverse/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:00.470Z","hash":"e0a6974032c1152bd8a17eaac4e21609a12c3c41227ba6ff0240f322dc7f5e76","originalBytes":15285,"storedBytes":15285,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["api","docs","search","articles","article","get","python","backend","postgresql","frontend","talk","diff","django","every","history","links","manage.py","red","security","architecture","docker","editor","nginx","npm","one","page","seed","what","build","changes","check","content","full-text","port","quality","revision","revisions","security.md","slug","stack","testing","without","architecture.md","between","contributing","decisions","